				<tr>
					<td class="windowbg2" colspan="3" valign="top" height="40">
						<div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13931#msg13931">Quote from: simplee on January 25, 2005, 05:18:57 pm</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1386.msg13925#msg13925">Quote from: Soltrack on January 25, 2005, 01:54:49 pm</a></div><div class="quote">I seem to remember it being friday and the alliance on sunday so as for your rotation RoS has been raiding time on Ascent&#039;s day also as for stepping in on Conviction you all had Tuesday if time had been cleared on Monday if not then wednesday and Thursday were your days and everyone then respected that is Ascent wanted Time on Friday it was theres so basically non of you have shit to bitch about.<br /></div><br />Periods, commas, and general punctuation might make this sentence readable.<br /></div><br />It is entirely readable and correct grammar makes no true difference. I suck at grammar so dont bother with it on a message board but the context is correct and relavent to this matter.
					</td>
				</tr>
